      "created_by_ref": "identity--8e4eb3a6-8119-430e-bf82-1d480fd3ce94",
      "name": "Load POWERSTAR backdoor in memory via remote-hosted decryption stage",
      "description": "Keep the POWERSTAR backdoor off disk and give the operator a remote kill switch over it. A malicious LNK runs cmd.exe to build an obfuscated PowerShell command that downloads a first-stage script from Backblaze B2 and runs it in memory through the Invoke-Expression alias 'gcm i*x'. A second remote script supplies the AES decryption routine and key; only then is the encrypted backdoor decrypted and run, and if that script is withdrawn the payload cannot be recovered. A defender sees cmd.exe spawning PowerShell with a wildcard Get-Command lookup and outbound HTTPS to backblazeb2.com.",
      "x_procedure_type": "reporting",
